.TH "DEDALUS\-LOGOUT" "1" "" "dedalus" "Dedalus Manual"
.SH "NAME"
dedalus\-logout \- forget saved credentials
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B dedalus logout
[\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIurl\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Removes the credentials saved for one base URL, or for every base URL. A credential supplied through a flag or an environment variable is not stored here, so it is not removed. It also asks the provider to revoke a saved OAuth token when a revocation endpoint is known. The local copy is removed first, so if the provider cannot be reached the credential is still gone from this machine; the failure is printed as a warning and the command still succeeds.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Forget every saved credential, for every base URL. Cannot be combined with \-\-base\-url, which names one.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIurl\fR
Forget the credentials saved for this base URL. Cannot be combined with \-\-all.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command completed successfully.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command was invoked incorrectly (missing or invalid arguments).
.TP
\fB10\fR
Sign\-in or sign\-out did not complete. The message on standard error says why.
